#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG9673 expect=violation domain=EC
#note "The sister half of the CDISC-CG0462 pair (minted 2026-09-11, M9/T1-32). ECDOSTXT is not in the dataset (None satisfied) while ECDOSE is present with missing values on both rows and ECOCCUR=Y, so the remaining condition holds on both rows (the ECSTAT leaf empty(ECSTAT) is true with no ECSTAT column - ECSTAT is not a variable of EC in any shipped IG, F15). Sensitivity is Dataset, so the absence is reported ONCE although both rows qualify. Same dataset shape as the parent's skipped_no_ecdostxt_column scenario: the parent skips, this rule reports."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset EC class=INTERVENTIONS label="Exposure as Collected"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ECSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ECTRT   type=Char label="Name of Treatment"
col ECOCCUR type=Char label="Occurrence"
col ECDOSE  type=Num  label="Dose"
---
S1 | EC | 001 | 1 | DRUG A | Y | .
S1 | EC | 001 | 2 | DRUG A | Y | .
